 "equipment_type": "Rooftop unit controller (gateway)",
 "applies_to": "Carrier WeatherExpert 48N and 50N (sizes N2-N9) large rooftop units with ComfortLink controls and the factory UPC Open BACnet option.",
 "summary": "On WeatherExpert 48/50N rooftops the BACnet option is a UPC Open controller that talks BACnet MS/TP to the BMS and CCN to the unit's ComfortLink board. The list has 164 AVs and BVs: occupancy, supply air and static pressure setpoints, air temperatures, pressures and flows, compressor and heat relays, economizer and VFD values, thermostat and switch inputs, demand limits, alarms and spare user values.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "Object names end in _1. Rows the table prints without an object ID (System Space AQ/RH/Temperature, Use Linkage, User Defined Analog 1 and 6-20) are left out.",
  "Access is from the READ/WRITE column; W-only rows (CCN forces such as Occupied?, Outside Air Temperature, thermostat inputs) are listed as writable.",
  "Units printed as °^F or ^F are shown as Δ°F (temperature differences); dF is shown as °F.",
  "The 48/50A and 48/50P lists use the same layout but share only about 100 of these objects, so this is a separate entry.",
  "Points depend on unit options (heat type, economizer, Humidi-MiZer, VFDs, airflow monitoring, controls expansion boards)."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "WeatherExpert 48N2-N9 and 50N2-N9 Single Package Rooftop Units - Controls, Start-Up, Operation, Service and Troubleshooting (Appendix F, BACnet Option Network Points List)",
  "doc_number": "48-50N-8T",
  "revision_date": "2022-03",
  "url": "https://www.shareddocs.com/hvac/docs/1005/Public/0F/48-50N-8T.pdf"
 },
 "integration": {
  "summary": "The BMS talks BACnet MS/TP to the UPC Open, which reads and writes the ComfortLink control over CCN. Set the CCN schedule number for the occupancy source you want, then write occupancy and (for VAV) the supply air and static pressure setpoints; read HVAC mode, temperatures and alarm state. Values the BMS feeds in (space, return or outdoor temperature, RH, IAQ) are forces that clear if not refreshed.",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
    "ref": "BV 2008",
    "name": "occ_status_1",
    "why": "Occupied? (0 = no, 1 = yes); writable"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 3007",
    "name": "sa_temp_stpt_1",
    "why": "Supply air setpoint (VAV units)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 3050",
    "name": "sa_static_stpt_1",
    "why": "Duct static pressure setpoint (VAV units)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 1022",
    "name": "hvac_mode_1",
    "why": "HVAC mode as a number"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 2050",
    "name": "sf_vfd_output_1",
    "why": "Supply fan VFD speed, %"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 43",
    "name": "ctrltemp_1",
    "why": "Control temperature (RAT, SPT or zone)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 10",
    "name": "sat_1",
    "why": "Supply air temperature leaving the fan"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 9",
    "name": "alm_1",
    "why": "Unit alarm state"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 105",
    "name": "comm_lost_alm_1",
    "why": "UPC lost CCN communication with the unit"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "Occupancy follows the ComfortLink CCN schedule number (SCH.N): 0 = always occupied, 1 = internal schedule, 65-99 = a broadcast global schedule. The points list makes Occupied? (BV 2008) writable, but the manual does not describe how a write interacts with SCH.N; test it on site. The unit ships with Local Machine Disable (BV 59 unitstop_1) set, which must be cleared before the unit runs.",
  "heartbeat": "The manual says CCN forces at priority 7 clear unless rewritten in time: outside air temperature, outside RH, outside air quality and static pressure reset after 30 minutes; return air and space temperature after 3 minutes.",
  "remote_sensors": "Space Temperature (AV 137), Return Air Temperature (AV 135), Outside Air Temperature (AV 1003), Outside Air RH (AV 119), IAQ (AV 1009) and OAQ (AV 113) are writable. Refresh them within the force timeouts (3 min for space and return temperature, 30 min for outdoor values).",
  "setup": [
   "Set the MAC address on the UPC Open Tens and Ones rotary switches; it reads switches, DIP switches and jumpers only at power-up.",
   "Device instance = network number (default 16101) followed by the MAC address, e.g. MAC 20 gives 1610120.",
   "BAS port: DS3 enable, DS4 E1-485, DS5-DS8 set to MSTP; baud on DS1-DS2 (9600, 19.2k, 38.4k or 76.8k, Carrier default 76.8k).",
   "Fit a BT485 terminator on the first and last controller of the MS/TP segment.",
   "The UPC Open and the ComfortLink board must use the same CCN element and bus numbers."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "Points depend on unit options; objects for options not fitted carry no useful data.",
   "Thermostat inputs (Y1, Y2, W1, W2, G) and switch inputs are writable BVs (CCN forces).",
   "The user-defined analog and binary values are spare objects with no unit function."
  ]
 },
